[
  {
    "role": "user",
    "content": "You are playing a text adventure game. I will describe what you can perceive in the game. You write the single action you want to take in the game starting with >. Write your plan for your next actions on the line below your action, starting with \"Next actions:\".\nFor example:\n> open cupboard\nNext actions: take orange, eat orange\n\nYou can have up to two objects in your inventory at the same time.\n\nYour goal for this game is: Put the pillow on the table, the book on the table and the plate on the table.\n\nOnce you have achieved your goal, write \"> done\" to end the game.\n\nYou are in a bedroom now. There are a pillow, a wardrobe and a bed. The pillow is on the bed. The wardrobe is closed. There is a passage to a living room here."
  },
  {
    "role": "user",
    "content": "> take pillow  \nNext actions: take pillow, go to living room, put pillow on table"
  },
  {
    "role": "user",
    "content": "You take the pillow. In your inventory you have a pillow.\n"
  },
  {
    "role": "user",
    "content": "You are a skilled planner. Above you see the game history. What would be the best next action? Openly reason about the next step, then produce your next action exactly as the game expects it preceded by the separator 'ACT:' on its own line."
  }
]
